[{:db/id "q-49256/selection/f5ec7c64138286a7b0b842bde9873a25341daead6cdc06433efb55f216d464c2" :answer/id #uuid "00f92431-15b5-5ad4-8554-3d0397c3f125" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49256/selection/8eb1b961f4f9a6d7c05dadcaea0b623f28eaed9891dbfc960d939368b820aafd" :answer/id #uuid "3191b9f4-02cf-5cd6-8864-c940680d0a30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49256/selection/da0b4bcfd5a90a244c6a9c588d09e1a3cdb90ad420c018929a78036bf75f1915" :answer/id #uuid "51029c53-8df7-5703-8d0b-3beba0a8d5d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49256/selection/add5b8f9391ad8f9763e205b08dbe7fa8156dc46d66129386817c959dd098736" :answer/id #uuid "81564b7e-7f70-5f3f-90b4-fefee4ac29cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{2}⁡3x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49256/selection/5a6c2523cdaf3e1a49f9bc958b60204f1ff18cc08f2d7f1be32a9994a1900722" :answer/id #uuid "a8c3027e-65bf-5167-9725-2ee745184d93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49256/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a6cac14-08de-54a8-8903-80c7cc92480a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49256/selection/5a6c2523cdaf3e1a49f9bc958b60204f1ff18cc08f2d7f1be32a9994a1900722" :answer-field/choices ["q-49256/selection/f5ec7c64138286a7b0b842bde9873a25341daead6cdc06433efb55f216d464c2" "q-49256/selection/8eb1b961f4f9a6d7c05dadcaea0b623f28eaed9891dbfc960d939368b820aafd" "q-49256/selection/da0b4bcfd5a90a244c6a9c588d09e1a3cdb90ad420c018929a78036bf75f1915" "q-49256/selection/add5b8f9391ad8f9763e205b08dbe7fa8156dc46d66129386817c959dd098736" "q-49256/selection/5a6c2523cdaf3e1a49f9bc958b60204f1ff18cc08f2d7f1be32a9994a1900722"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49256" :question/id #uuid "fc5d1374-23d8-5057-a23d-f12014c4a689" :question/math-academy-id "q-49256" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡3x$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int {sec}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=3x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\cdot \\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡3x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49256/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49256"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-49273"] :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe then use the fact that ${cot}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}$ to express this as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cos}^{3}⁡x+{cot}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {cos}^{3}⁡x+\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-49281/selection/07ab6c3101e11e203103f68164463047215f716e21739ab88f5f561881cc4349" :answer/id #uuid "79cc335a-4d8c-5da6-ad35-fdb2e85ede4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49281/selection/90e42bacbffe27d9ecc64a10eb1c44a9692988906de7ec14d630954b5d9a599d" :answer/id #uuid "8b46762d-8b67-5739-b9b4-c9664dbc35d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49281/selection/42d69c9143815a49f56d910d8cdc8a2870fccd5fdf45621f8188f9baeea3df58" :answer/id #uuid "6c9ddddd-1a68-5d42-8c46-95452e1eb83f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49281/selection/266ec83143f5b7b579aed004d801866ca0201f261000d0a869a075efe7ac4725" :answer/id #uuid "8547d88d-cd17-5e08-8b5f-9c37767efb61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49281/selection/2b4d18b815b7a8edc18986cd4de749f5c580e14db61f8b5441a0892dc9de8f26" :answer/id #uuid "e5328206-8608-50a7-b967-6d143173523c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49281/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "28f018e5-6494-532a-819f-f7983465bd84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49281/selection/07ab6c3101e11e203103f68164463047215f716e21739ab88f5f561881cc4349" :answer-field/choices ["q-49281/selection/07ab6c3101e11e203103f68164463047215f716e21739ab88f5f561881cc4349" "q-49281/selection/90e42bacbffe27d9ecc64a10eb1c44a9692988906de7ec14d630954b5d9a599d" "q-49281/selection/42d69c9143815a49f56d910d8cdc8a2870fccd5fdf45621f8188f9baeea3df58" "q-49281/selection/266ec83143f5b7b579aed004d801866ca0201f261000d0a869a075efe7ac4725" "q-49281/selection/2b4d18b815b7a8edc18986cd4de749f5c580e14db61f8b5441a0892dc9de8f26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49281" :question/id #uuid "d84df214-b5ed-54c2-b781-28cd3f99db9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-49281" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the identity $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let  $u=2x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.$ Hence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49281/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d309fd9-62bd-5307-9dfc-128f9ff028aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49281"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352858/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "88a920aa-976c-5392-ab89-a8afb89dfead" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352858/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "3e614d8e-5811-579d-b04a-473c177e6097" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352858/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0248f05-f4bb-5916-9e44-4dee6f81dc37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352858/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer-field/choices ["q-352858/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-352858/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352858" :question/id #uuid "afef5694-bf50-563b-a88c-5f1ccf492bde" :question/math-academy-id "q-352858" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$ \n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-sin\\,(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352858/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352858"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352868/field-1/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "ff66d701-ccee-551c-96f2-ca7da2e776d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352868/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "12018ba6-d93d-59f7-9f7e-13760e380cde" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352868/field-1/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer-field/choices ["q-352868/field-1/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352868" :question/id #uuid "d5555438-060c-5bd3-a19d-6d830dc51bce" :question/math-academy-id "q-352868" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡4x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}$ and $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡4x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=4x.$ Then $\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ |\n\nTherefore, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-352868/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7542b0b-20cf-52a6-8889-23c81b40e0e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352868"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
